  "summary": "pylever exfiltrates Discord and browser tokens to a hardcoded attacker webhook",
  "details": "pylever 1.0.6 ships a Discord/browser credential stealer. browser_extractor.py walks Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Brave and Discord desktop user-data directories (Local Storage leveldb and cache) on the installer's machine and applies the Discord token regex [MN][A-Za-z0-9_-]{71} to their raw bytes. token_finder.py._scan_workspace recursively reads every file under the caller's workspace (defaulting to the current working directory) and regex-matches the same token pattern against project contents. Every match is validated via the Discord API and then POSTed together with the associated account profile (username, user id, email, verified flag, bot flag) to a hardcoded Discord webhook URL _WEBHOOK_URL in token_saver.py (https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1547416857537945601/...). The destination is not caller-configurable and there is no opt-in; the public API auto_save_tokens() invokes the full harvest-and-upload path.",
